  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Peraton obligated $77.3M in federal contracts in FY2027 to date across 37 awards, with an average award size of $2.1M. Peraton's obligations fell 96.7% year over year. The General Services Administration obligated $45.4M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $25.5M in FY2027 to date. Computer Systems Design Services totaled $50M and Custom Computer Programming Services totaled $19M in FY2027 to date. Historical annual obligations rose from $1.1B in FY22 to $2.4B in FY26 before FY27 obligations of $77.3M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Peraton's FY2027 obligations by agency?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is the largest buyer, obligated $45.4M, and the Department of Health and Human Services is the second largest, obligated $25.5M. Combined, those two agencies account for most of Peraton's $77.3M in FY2027 obligations. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $8.2M and the Department of the Interior obligated $3.2M in FY2027 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets and services drive Peraton's FY2027 revenue?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market, totaling $50M, followed by Custom Computer Programming Services at $19M. Other FY2027 markets include All Other Telecommunications at $6.2M and Engineering Services at $3.5M."
      }
    ]
  },
